### 8. **WebSocket Authentication Race Condition**

**Location:** Lines 237-247  
**Severity:** **HIGH**

**Failure Mechanism:**
```javascript
httpsServer.on("upgrade", (req, socket, head) => {
  if (!checkAuth(req)) {
    socket.end(/* ... */);
    return;
  }
  proxy.proxyWebSocket(req, socket, head, CANVAS_TARGET);
});
```

**Exploit Scenario:**
1. WebSocket upgrade happens before full request validation
2. `checkAuth` may have race conditions with cookie parsing
3. No validation of WebSocket subprotocol
4. Missing origin header validation

**Refactored Code:**
```javascript
// Lines 237-247 REPLACEMENT:
httpsServer.on("upgrade", (req, socket, head) => {
  // Validate WebSocket upgrade request
  if (req.headers.upgrade?.toLowerCase() !== "websocket") {
    socket.end("HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\r\n\r\n");
    return;
  }

  // Validate origin header (prevent cross-origin WebSocket attacks)
  const origin = req.headers.origin;
  if (LAN_AUTH_ENABLED && origin) {
    try {
      const originUrl = new URL(origin);
      const expectedHost = req.headers.host;
      if (originUrl.hostname !== expectedHost?.split(":")[0]) {
        socket.end("HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden\r\n\r\n");
        return;
      }
    } catch {
      socket.end("HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden\r\n\r\n");
      return;
    }
  }

  // Validate authentication
  if (!checkAuth(req)) {
    socket.end(
      "HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized\r\n" +
      "Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\r\n" +
      "Connection: close\r\n" +
      "\r\n" +
      "Требуется авторизация\r\n"
    );
    return;
  }

  // Validate WebSocket subprotocol
  const secWebSocketProtocol = req.headers["sec-websocket-protocol"];
  if (secWebSocketProtocol && !["openhands-protocol", "chat"].includes(secWebSocketProtocol)) {
    socket.end("HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\r\n\r\n");
    return;
  }

  proxy.proxyWebSocket(req, socket, head, CANVAS_TARGET);
});
```

---

### 9. **Hardcoded Default PFX Passphrase**

**Location:** Line 25  
**Severity:** **HIGH**

**Failure Mechanism:**
```javascript
const PFX_PASS = process.env.OPENHANDS_PFX_PASSPHRASE || "openhands-pwa-local";
```

**Exploit Scenario:**
1. Default passphrase is predictable
2. If PFX file is stolen, attacker can decrypt it with known passphrase
3. Passphrase should never be hardcoded

**Refactored Code:**
```javascript
// Line 25 REPLACEMENT:
const PFX_PASS = process.env.OPENHANDS_PFX_PASSPHRASE;
if (!PFX_PASS) {
  console.error("[LAN Gateway] CRITICAL: OPENHANDS_PFX_PASSPHRASE environment variable not set");
  console.error("[LAN Gateway] Certificate passphrase must be configured via environment variable");
  process.exit(1);
}
```

